entries.description:
A set can also be described by writing a description of its elements between curly brackets. Thus the set S can also be written as:
S = {odd whole numbers less than 10}
which we read as ‘S is the set of odd whole numbers less than 10’.

If an element is listed more than once, it is only counted once. For example:
{a, a, b} = {a, b}
because the set {a, a, b} has only the two elements ‘a’ and ‘b’. It is normally considered poor notation to list an element more than once.
